'''Shibalien''' (エイリワン, ''Eiriwan'', '''Aliwan''') is an [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] variant of [[Doge]] that appears in [[Into the Future]], [[Cats of the Cosmos]] and [[Legend Stages]]. He was added in [[Version 4.0 Update|Version 4.0]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Shibalien
|image = E 167.png
|first appearance = '''ItF''': [[Japan (Into the Future)|Chapter 1 - Japan]]<br>
'''SoL''': [[Valkyrie Plains|Sub-Chapter 25 - Valkyrie Plains]]<br>
'''CotC''': [[Mars (Cats of the Cosmos)|Chapter 1 - Mars]]
|latest appearance = '''ZL''': [[Coral Housing|Sub-chapter 19 - Coral Housing]]
|money drop = 90¢ - 355¢
}}

==Enemy==
As the first Alien enemy encountered, Shibalien poses little to no threat outside of his first few appearances and is usually just there to take a hit for stronger enemies, although at high buffs he can survive the [[Cat Cannon]]. Using two [[Cow Cat (Normal Cat)|Lion Cats]] or one [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Sexy Legs Cat]] can get the job done fast.

==Strategy==
When you first encounter him in [[Japan (Into the Future)|Japan]], do not underestimate him, as he can easily kill your frontline cats. However, ranged cats like [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]] or [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Sexy Legs Cat]] can dish out lots of damage and eventually kill him. Even [[Bird Cat (Normal Cat)|UFO Cat]] can be a decent option if protected with meatshields. If you use [[Valkyrie Cat (Special Cat)|Valkyrie Cat]] or [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]], this enemy should be trivially easy.

Later on, or when you have more [[Into the Future]] treasures, just treat him like a Doge with a different design.

